        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d2394ded-5106-503d-9f81-2aff586403e0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Havanese, Black Mouth Cur, Poodle\n- Dog breed ancestry and types: Bichon type, Blanquito de la Habana, Havana Silk Dogs\n- Places: Cuba, Havana, Southern United States\n- Dog grooming: Cording\n\nFacts:\n- The Havanese is a breed of Bichon type.\n- The Havanese is the national dog of Cuba.\n- The Havanese was developed from the now extinct Blanquito de la Habana, meaning \"little white dog of Havana.\"\n- Havana Silk Dogs was originally another name for the Blanquito de la Habana.\n- The Black Mouth Cur originated in the Southern United States.\n- The Black Mouth Cur is a hunting and cattle dog.\n- In dog grooming, the Havanese and Poodle are occasionally corded for showing.",
